# Keeping the OFFER line on a scan roughly true.
#
# A science tab is a stored string: the scan writes it once and re-selecting the contact
# never runs that block again. So something has to push - the same arrangement
# science_status.mast documents, and for the same reason.
#
# SLOW on purpose. The status line tracks a shield coming back and ticks every second;
# work on offer changes when a job is granted or taken, which is minutes apart. A fast
# walk here would cost the sim a great deal to write the same string over and over.
#
# //shared/signal, not //signal: the write is indexed by the SCANNING SIDE, so one
# console doing it is the whole side done. Five consoles each starting a watcher is five
# tickers writing the same blob. SIGNAL_ROUTING.md.

default shared OFFER_SCAN_LINE = True

//shared/signal/game_started if OFFER_SCAN_LINE
    task_schedule(science_offers_watch)


=== science_offers_watch
" Refresh the offer line on contacts this side has already scanned.
--- science_offers_beat
    await delay_sim(20)
    lm_science_offers_tick()
    jump science_offers_beat
